al: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The artifact-file store can be measured, drained, and bounded: [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sase artifact stats` reports its economics, `sase artifact prune` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and `sase artifact reclaim` are dry-run by default and route every [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]removal through a restorable trash, an opt-in `artifacts.retention`[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]policy keeps the store bounded going forward, and nothing an agent [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]declared or a bead, plan, or ChangeSpec references is ever removed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifact_store_lifecycle.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ba[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ba/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core: store economics, retention planner, and trash [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]primitives[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-lifecycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-lifecycle: add a pure store-economics aggregator, a pure retention [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planner, and clock-free trash store/list/restore/purge primitives to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase_core`, expose all four through `sase_core_rs`, and release the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]crate.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Store economics report and the protected-reference scan[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-report[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-lifecycle[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py-report: raise the `sase-core-rs` pin, add the Python bridges for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]economics and retention planning, add the bead/plan/ChangeSpec reference[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scan that produces protected artifact ids, and ship `sase artifact [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stats` as a read-only report with a JSON mode.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Dry-run-first pruning and the trash lifecycle[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-prune[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-report[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py-prune: add `sase artifact prune` (dry run unless `--apply`) and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase artifact trash {list,purge,restore}` group, with index-row removal[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and restoration performed under the existing index lock and every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]removal routed through the trash.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retroactive version-control reclaim of the pooled bytes[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-reclaim[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-prune[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py-reclaim: add `sase artifact reclaim`, which converts stored automatic[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows whose exact content is reproducible from a durable ref into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]byte-free VCS-backed rows and trashes the redundant copies, reusing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture policy's git probe and verifying by digest first.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Opt-in retention configuration and enforcement[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]retention-config[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-prune[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]retention-config: add the `artifacts.retention` configuration block [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]defaulting to disabled, its schema entries and accessors, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bounded, fail-safe enforcement pass that runs after automatic capture at[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]finalization and purges expired trash.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, skill, and configuration reference[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-and-skill[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-reclaim, retention-config[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-and-skill: document the store lifecycle, the new subcommands, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trash contract, and the retention block across the CLI, configuration, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and artifact docs, and refresh the `sase_artifact_file` skill source and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its deployed copy.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ba","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-ba.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-163254d0efbba308521b85865a89d938","started_at":"2026-07-30T14:42:54.371891+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785433561,"sha":"ac2d5b22cf2d4cc0c0c25f5accb039d9118cee79","subject":"feat(artifact): reclaim stored bytes from durable VCS"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"43834635b773dcdefa77523a82fac5fdbb4b7f3400e35c2e33438f5ad10e5cf2","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ba.4/chat.md","size_bytes":12196},"commits":{"digest":"48151259df3c5cd65d0757a58c8b466e49db4993423adff5cef718d4bf1b23da","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ba.4/commits.json","size_bytes":231},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ba.4/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"881dbf69244b1fd7898fe4857f3883525a4fab1d3abd441a03cc494783db6a51","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ba.4/meta.json","size_bytes":603},"prompt":{"digest":"21831bb9e5a27e215444